---
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { t, pathFor, type Lang } from '../i18n';
interface Props { lang: Lang }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const c = t(lang);
const mail = SITE.contactEmail;
---
<article class="legal wrap narrow">
  {lang === 'zh' ? (
    <Fragment>
      <h1>隐私政策</h1>
      <div class="draft-banner" role="note"><strong>{c.legal.draft}</strong><br />{c.legal.draftBody}</div>
      <p class="muted small">{c.legal.updated}：2026-10-07</p>

      <h2>1. 适用范围</h2>
      <p>本政策适用于本网站和千剪 Reelfold 开源软件（桌面应用和 video-studio 技能）。千剪免费、按 MIT 许可开源，由［维护者 / 运营主体，待填］维护。联系邮箱：<a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>。</p>

      <h2>2. 浏览本网站</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>本站是静态网站，不使用 cookie，不加载统计或广告脚本，不从第三方加载字体，也没有表单。</li>
        <li>托管服务商（Cloudflare）可能按其政策记录访问日志，例如 IP 地址和浏览器信息。我们不会用这些日志识别个人。</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. 桌面应用和开源技能</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>软件在你自己的电脑上运行。视频和音频文件默认留在本机，语音转写和渲染在本机完成。我们没有服务器接收你的素材。</li>
        <li>为了选段、写标题和校对字幕，逐字稿文本、少量关键帧截图和标题会发给你自己配置的 AI 服务（你的 Claude Code / Codex 订阅、你的 API key，或本地模型）。用 AI 配音或 AI 视频生成时，文本和参考图会发给对应厂商。这些数据按你和该服务商之间的条款处理。</li>
        <li>引擎用到的 MediaPipe 组件可能会向 Google 上报匿名使用统计，应用里会说明这一点和关闭方法。</li>
        <li>检查更新时，应用会访问 GitHub 上的发布页面。</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. 联系我们和 GitHub</h2>
      <p>你发给我们的邮件只用于回复你。在 GitHub Discussions 或 Issues 里发的内容是公开的，按 GitHub 的条款处理，请不要贴出私人素材或密钥。</p>

      <h2>5. 你的权利</h2>
      <p>你可以要求查看或删除你发给我们的邮件中的个人信息。发邮件到 <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>，我们会在 7 天内处理并回复确认。</p>

      <h2>6. 变更</h2>
      <p>政策变更时，我们会更新本页日期。</p>
      <p><a href={pathFor(lang)}>{c.legal.back}</a></p>
    </Fragment>
  ) : (
    <div lang={lang !== 'en' ? 'en' : undefined}>
      {lang !== 'en' && <p class="draft-banner" lang={lang} role="note">{c.legal.englishOnly}</p>}
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <div class="draft-banner" role="note"><strong>{c.legal.draft}</strong><br />{c.legal.draftBody}</div>
      <p class="muted small">{c.legal.updated}: 2026-10-07</p>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>This policy covers this website and the Reelfold open-source software (the desktop app and the video-studio skill). Reelfold is free and open source under the MIT licence, maintained by [maintainer / operating entity, to be filled in]. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. Visiting this website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>This is a static site. It sets no cookies, loads no analytics or ad scripts, loads no third-party fonts and has no forms.</li>
        <li>The hosting provider (Cloudflare) may keep access logs, such as IP address and browser details, under its own policy. We do not use those logs to identify people.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Desktop app and open-source skill</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The software runs on your own computer. Video and audio files stay there by default; transcription and rendering run locally. We run no server that receives your footage.</li>
        <li>To pick segments, write titles and proofread captions, transcript text, a few keyframe screenshots and titles are sent to the AI service you configure (your Claude Code or Codex subscription, your API keys, or a local model). AI voiceover or AI video generation sends text and reference images to that vendor. That is governed by your terms with the vendor.</li>
        <li>The MediaPipe component used by the engine may send anonymous usage statistics to Google; the app explains this and how to turn it off.</li>
        <li>When it checks for updates, the app contacts the release page on GitHub.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Contacting us and GitHub</h2>
      <p>Emails you send us are used only to reply to you. Anything you post in GitHub Discussions or Issues is public and handled under GitHub’s terms; please don’t post private footage or keys there.</p>

      <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see or delete personal data in emails you sent us. Email <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>; we act within 7 days and confirm by reply.</p>

      <h2>6. Changes</h2>
      <p>We update the date on this page when the policy changes.</p>
      <p><a href={pathFor(lang)}>{c.legal.back}</a></p>
    </div>
  )}
</article>
